Or, if you use cgconﬁg to manage cgroups, you can instead conﬁgure the cgroup's subsystems to support both LSF cgroup features by adding the
following to /etc/cgconﬁg.conf:
mount {
 freezer = /cgroup/freezer;
 cpuset = /cgroup/cpuset;
 cpuacct = /cgroup/cpuacct;
 memory = /cgroup/memory;
}
To start or restart the cgconﬁg service, use /etc/init.d/cgconﬁg start|restart.

